# Trained weight files are written by every run INCLUDING smoke tests, so
# they are not tracked by default — an 8-genome, 1-generation smoke result
# sitting in the repo looks exactly like a real one, and the whole point of
# weights.js refusing an uncommented non-zero is that a number has to carry
# the run that earned it.
#
# A result worth keeping gets committed deliberately, with its provenance
# in the commit message: git add -f trained.<mode>.json
trained.*.json

# The generic name is SCRATCH. Every run overwrites trained.<mode>.json,
# including the run you started five minutes ago, so a result kept under
# that name is a result waiting to be silently replaced — and it showed up
# as a phantom "uncommitted change" every time a new run finished, which is
# noise that trains you to ignore the warning.
#
# A result worth keeping is renamed by rounds.sh to
# trained.<mode>.<tag>.<runid>.r<N>.json and is tracked, because it is the
# only copy of an hour of compute and nothing else can reproduce it.
#
# THIS PATTERN MUST MATCH WHAT rounds.sh ACTUALLY WRITES. It read
# `!trained.*.round*.json` for a long time while rounds.sh named its output
# `...r1.json` — `r1` is not `round1`, so the exception never fired once and
# every real champion was silently ignored. A container restart then killed
# a crank mid-round and the surviving champion turned out to be untracked:
# an hour of compute was one restart from being unrecoverable, and nothing
# had said so, because a file that is ignored looks exactly like a file that
# is committed in `git status`.
#
# training.test.js asserts a name rounds.sh really produces is not ignored,
# so this pattern cannot drift away from the filenames again.
!trained.*.r[0-9]*.json
!trained.*.round*.json

# Void results from before the 15-feature registry — see its README.
void-pre-15-feature/

# THE CRANK'S RUNTIME STATE. Neither of these is ever committed.
#
# .crank-running means "a crank is alive IN THIS CONTAINER and did not choose
# to stop" — it is liveness, not configuration. Committing it would be worse
# than untidy: a fresh container cloning the repo would find a marker with no
# crank behind it, and session-start-resume-training.sh would faithfully start
# hours of training nobody asked for.
#
# crank.log is append-only for the life of a run and says nothing a champion
# file does not already carry.
.crank-running
crank.log
